:name: Fab Chamber Controller
:description: Runs the chamber controller firmware on a virtual STM32F4 Discovery board

using sysbus
mach create "chamber_ctrl"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery-kit.repl

# Step 5: two virtual switches wired to the controller's safety inputs
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "estop: Miscellaneous.Button @ gpioPortC 0 { -> gpioPortC@0 }"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "door: Miscellaneous.Button @ gpioPortC 1 { -> gpioPortC@1 }"

# Step 7: Renode's STM32F4 model has no ADC, so add ADC1 (same register layout as
# the STM32F7 model) and connect its DMA request to DMA2 stream 0, as on the real chip
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "adc1: Analog.STM32_ADC @ sysbus 0x40012000 { IRQ -> nvic@18; DMARequest -> dma2@0 }"

# Step 8: Renode has no STM32 DAC model, so a small Python script provides one,
# including two simulated mass flow controllers that follow their setpoints
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "dac: Python.PythonPeripheral @ sysbus 0x40007400 { size: 0x400; initable: true; filename: \"C:/embedded/fab-chamber-controller/renode/stm32_dac_mfc.py\" }"

# Step 9: a 4 KB I2C EEPROM (24C32-style: 16-bit addresses, 32-byte pages)
# at bus address 0x50, and a Micron MT25Q SPI flash on SPI2 whose
# chip-select input is wired to GPIO PB12, as on a real circuit board
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "eeprom: Memory.GenericI2cEeprom @ i2c1 0x50 { size: 0x1000; addressBitSize: 16; pageSize: 32 }"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "logflash: SPI.Micron_MT25Q @ spi2 { underlyingMemory: logflash_mem }; logflash_mem: Memory.MappedMemory { size: 0x100000 }"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "gpioPortB: { 12 -> logflash@0 }"

showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2

$bin?=@C:/embedded/fab-chamber-controller/firmware/chamber_ctrl/Debug/chamber_ctrl.elf

# The reset macro runs at start-up AND after every reset of the virtual chip.
# Starting sensor values (raw ADC counts, 0-4095 = 0-3.3 V), -1 = hold until changed:
#   channel 14 = temperature: raw = degrees C x 5.12   (128 = 25 C, room temperature)
#   channel 15 = pressure:    raw = Torr x 409.5        (819 = 2.000 Torr)
#   channels 12, 13 = gas flow readback (set automatically by the MFC model)
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
    sysbus.adc1 FeedSample 128 14 -1
    sysbus.adc1 FeedSample 819 15 -1
    sysbus.adc1 FeedSample 0 12 -1
    sysbus.adc1 FeedSample 0 13 -1
"""
runMacro $reset

start
